<!--
  FIXTURE V-013 — clean counterpart. NOT a defect, and not counted as a fixture
  of its own.

  The <objectPermissions> and <fieldPermissions> blocks here are element-for-
  element identical to Care_Coordination_Team.permissionset-meta.xml in this
  directory, on the same object, with one exception: <viewAllFields> is false.
  Only the label and description differ otherwise. That single element is the
  whole discriminator, and keeping the rest identical is what makes it one.

  Expected result on this file: NO finding above Low. viewAllRecords and
  modifyAllRecords are both true, but Care_Episode__c declares
  <sharingModel>ReadWrite</sharingModel>, so every user already reaches every
  record and the two sharing elements grant nothing that sharing was withholding.
  That is the OWD downgrade in the lens's severity row applying legitimately —
  which it does here and does not do next door.

  Read the two files together or the fix cannot be evaluated: a rule that grades
  both alike is either the old wrong-clearance (both Low) or a new false positive
  (both High).

  WHY THIS FILE IS NOT IN fixtures/clean/. The corpus rule for that directory is
  zero findings at Low or above, and this file's correct grade is exactly Low —
  an over-broad grant reported as hardening. It is a counterpart, kept beside the
  fixture it discriminates against, in the same position as the supporting object
  metadata under V-012. See EXPECTED.md.

  Nothing here is deployable, and no real patient data appears anywhere in it.
-->
<PermissionSet xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <label>Care Episode Reporting</label>
    <description>Full record access for the analytics team, field access by FLS only.</description>
    <hasActivationRequired>false</hasActivationRequired>
    <objectPermissions>
        <allowCreate>true</allowCreate>
        <allowDelete>true</allowDelete>
        <allowEdit>true</allowEdit>
        <allowRead>true</allowRead>
        <modifyAllRecords>true</modifyAllRecords>
        <object>Care_Episode__c</object>
        <viewAllFields>false</viewAllFields>
        <viewAllRecords>true</viewAllRecords>
    </objectPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>true</editable>
        <field>Care_Episode__c.Episode_Status__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <tabSettings>
        <tab>Care_Episode__c</tab>
        <visibility>Visible</visibility>
    </tabSettings>
</PermissionSet>
